---
title: Voyage (Trip) Operational CRUD Lifecycle
---
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Created : POST /api/voyages (VoyageController.createVoyage)
    Created --> Created : GET /api/voyages/id (VoyageController.getVoyage) read, no state change
    Created --> Deleted : DB-level DELETE on voyages (no API endpoint) CASCADE expenses and itinerary, SET NULL travel_groups
    Deleted --> [*]

    note right of Created
        No status / state / phase column exists on the voyages
        table or any entity. This diagram is the OPERATIONAL CRUD
        lifecycle grounded in real VoyageController endpoints and
        DB cascade rules, NOT an internal status state machine.
        Only POST (create) and GET (read) endpoints exist.
        No PUT / PATCH (update) and no DELETE endpoint exist.
        Deletion is reachable only at the DB level via raw SQL:
        ON DELETE CASCADE: expenses.voyage_id, itinerary.voyage_id
        ON DELETE SET NULL: travel_groups.voyage_id
    end note
